You have strabismic amblyopia. This means vision in one eye did not develop normally in childhood because the eyes were not aligned.\
\
When one eye turns, the brain may ignore the image from that eye to avoid double vision. Over time, the turned eye does not develop normal visual sharpness, even if the eye itself is structurally healthy.\
\
